      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your concern highlights the profound tension between preventing future suffering and avoiding the self-righteous danger of preemptive wars. While waiting for explicit atrocities often leaves too much time for despotism to flourish, history demonstrates that well-intentioned pre-emptive strikes frequently create international instability and de-humane causality. A truly robust justice framework requires an overwhelming consensus of evidence regarding imminent mass harm to avoid imperial overreach, as ignoring the risks of error can inadvertently worsen the very tyranny society seeks to end.",
